<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Supplementary Material</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1. </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide our annealing scheduler training algorithm in Alg.<a href="#algorithm1" title="In A.1. Implementation Details ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Navigating with Annealing Guidance Scale in Diffusion Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and its inference algorithm in Alg.<a href="#algorithm4" title="In A.1. Implementation Details ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Navigating with Annealing Guidance Scale in Diffusion Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
Our annealing scheduler <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\theta}(t,z_{t},\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\theta}(t,z_{t},\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is implemented as a lightweight MLP with three hidden layers of dimension 128, resulting in a total of 52K trainable parameters. The model takes as input sinusoidal embeddings of three features: (1) the normalized timestep <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t/T</annotation></semantics></math>, (2) the normalized guidance magnitude <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta_{t}\|/\|\delta\|_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta_{t}\|/\|\delta\|_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta\|_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mtext>max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta\|_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the typical maximum norm of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> observed empirically across the training set and set to 5.0 in SDXL, and (3) the prompt-alignment parameter <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Each embedding is 4-dimensional, and the three embeddings are concatenated before being passed through the first layer. ReLU activations are applied after each layer. The network outputs a single scalar corresponding to the predicted guidance scale. When we constrain the guidance scale <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> in the ablation to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> we add a sigmoid layer at the output. Training is performed for a maximum of 20,000 steps using the AdamW optimizer with a learning rate of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\text{e}{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>e</mtext></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\text{e}{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> and weight decay of 0.01. We train with a per-device batch size of 2 and accumulate gradients for 8 steps before performing an optimizer update. We use the default Kaiming-uniform initialization. All training runs complete within approximately 4.5 hours on a single NVIDIA A6000 GPU (48GB).</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ALGORITHM 1</span> </span>Annealing Scheduler - Training</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">

<span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Require :</span>  <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>: <span id="algorithm1.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">trainable</span> guidance scale model;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{(\cdot)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{(\cdot)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: <span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">frozen</span> noise predictor, accepts <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> or a condition, at timestep <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>: total number of denoising steps

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">repeat</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">--- Sample data and noise --- </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Sample <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{z}_{0},\mathbf{c})\sim p(\mathbf{z}_{0},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{z}_{0},\mathbf{c})\sim p(\mathbf{z}_{0},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim U[1,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim U[1,T]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\epsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\epsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\sim[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\sim[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}\leftarrow\text{AddNoise}(\mathbf{z}_{0},t,\boldsymbol{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>AddNoise</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}\leftarrow\text{AddNoise}(\mathbf{z}_{0},t,\boldsymbol{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{c}}\leftarrow\text{Perturb}(\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Perturb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{c}}\leftarrow\text{Perturb}(\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">--- Step at time <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> --- </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\tilde{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\tilde{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon^{\varnothing}_{t}(\mathbf{z}_{t})+w_{\theta}(t,\delta_{t},\lambda)\cdot\left(\epsilon_{t}^{\tilde{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon^{\varnothing}_{t}(\mathbf{z}_{t})+w_{\theta}(t,\delta_{t},\lambda)\cdot\left(\epsilon_{t}^{\tilde{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>  ;  <span id="algorithm1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CFG</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0|t}=(z_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\hat{\epsilon}_{t})/\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0|t}=(z_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\hat{\epsilon}_{t})/\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Denoise</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t-1}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}z_{0|t}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t-1}=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}z_{0|t}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Renoise</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">--- Step at time <math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math> --- </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t-1}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\tilde{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t-1})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t-1}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\tilde{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t-1})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">--- Compute loss and update --- </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\lambda\|\delta_{t-1}\|^{2}+(1-\lambda)\|\boldsymbol{\epsilon}-\hat{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}_{t}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\lambda\|\delta_{t-1}\|^{2}+(1-\lambda)\|\boldsymbol{\epsilon}-\hat{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}_{t}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Take gradient step on <math id="algorithm1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm1.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Update scheduler</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.19" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">until</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.19.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">converged</em>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.20" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ALGORITHM 2</span> </span>CFG - Inference (DDIM)</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">

<span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Require :</span>  <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>: total number of denoising steps;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>: guidance scale;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{(\cdot)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{(\cdot)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: <span id="algorithm2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">frozen</span> noise predictor, accepts <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> or a condition, at timestep <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math>: condition;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.4.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})+w\cdot(\epsilon_{t}^{\mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>𝐜</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})+w\cdot(\epsilon_{t}^{\mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>;  <span id="algorithm2.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CFG</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0|t}\leftarrow(\mathbf{z}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\cdot\hat{\epsilon}_{t})/\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0|t}\leftarrow(\mathbf{z}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\cdot\hat{\epsilon}_{t})/\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm2.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Denoise</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t-1}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot z_{0|t}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot\hat{\epsilon}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t-1}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot z_{0|t}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot\hat{\epsilon}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm2.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Renoise</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.10" class="ltx_listingline">end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.11.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ALGORITHM 3</span> </span>CFG++ - Inference (DDIM)</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm3.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">

<span id="algorithm3.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Require :</span>  <math id="algorithm3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>: total number of denoising steps;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>: guidance scale;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{(\cdot)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{(\cdot)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: <span id="algorithm3.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">frozen</span> noise predictor, accepts <math id="algorithm3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> or a condition, at timestep <math id="algorithm3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math>: condition;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm3.4.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm3.4.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm3.4.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})+w\cdot(\epsilon_{t}^{\mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>𝐜</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})+w\cdot(\epsilon_{t}^{\mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>;  <span id="algorithm3.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm3.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CFG</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0|t}\leftarrow(\mathbf{z}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\cdot\hat{\epsilon}_{t})/\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0|t}\leftarrow(\mathbf{z}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\cdot\hat{\epsilon}_{t})/\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm3.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm3.4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Denoise</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t-1}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot z_{0|t}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot\boldsymbol{\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>𝒕</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∅</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝒕</mi></msub><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t-1}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot z_{0|t}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot\boldsymbol{\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm3.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm3.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Renoise</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.10" class="ltx_listingline">end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="algorithm3.4.11.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="algorithm4" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ALGORITHM 4</span> </span>Annealing Scheduler - Inference (DDIM)</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm4.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">

<span id="algorithm4.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Require :</span>  <math id="algorithm4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>: prompt alignment weighting parameter;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>: total number of denoising steps;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>: <span id="algorithm4.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">trained</span> guidance scale model;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{(\cdot)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{(\cdot)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: <span id="algorithm4.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">frozen</span> noise predictor, accepts <math id="algorithm4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> or a condition, at timestep <math id="algorithm4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math>: condition;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.7.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm4.4.7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.4.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\tilde{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\tilde{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})+\boldsymbol{w_{\theta}(t,\|\delta_{t}\|,\lambda)}\cdot(\epsilon_{t}^{\mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mi>𝒕</mi></msub><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>𝐜</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}_{t}\leftarrow\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})+\boldsymbol{w_{\theta}(t,\|\delta_{t}\|,\lambda)}\cdot(\epsilon_{t}^{\mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{z}_{t})-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>;  <span id="algorithm4.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm4.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CFG</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0|t}\leftarrow(\mathbf{z}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\cdot\hat{\epsilon}_{t})/\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0|t}\leftarrow(\mathbf{z}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\cdot\hat{\epsilon}_{t})/\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm4.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm4.4.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Denoise</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t-1}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot z_{0|t}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot\boldsymbol{\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>𝒕</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∅</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝒕</mi></msub><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t-1}\leftarrow\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot z_{0|t}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot\boldsymbol{\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}(\mathbf{z}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm4.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm4.4.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Renoise</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.12" class="ltx_listingline">end for
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="algorithm4.4.13.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2. </span>Training Data</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the LAION-POP subset of LAION-5B dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schuhmann et al., 2022</a>)</cite> with high-resolution images with detailed descriptions, and selected 20,000 images based on the highest similarity scores.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3. </span>Memory and Time Consumption</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluated the inference time of our lightweight model, which has a footprint of only 700KB. Running the model 10,000 times on a NVIDIA RTX A5000 yielded a mean inference time of 0.001434 seconds with a standard deviation of 0.000123 seconds. Given that the model is activated for 50 timesteps during a typical diffusion process, this results in an additional computational cost of approximately <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0717" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.0717</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0717</annotation></semantics></math> seconds per sample.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4. </span>Intuition for <math id="A1.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-loss</h3>

<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2506.24108v1/intuition.png" id="A1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/407;" width="476" height="407" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>. </span><span id="A1.F11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Intuition behind the <math id="A1.F11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-loss.<span id="A1.F11.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> A 2D illustration showing how the magnitude of <math id="A1.F11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}=\epsilon_{t}^{c}-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}=\epsilon_{t}^{c}-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math> reflects alignment with the prompt. At time <math id="A1.F11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the sample <math id="A1.F11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0|t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false" mathsize="1.580em">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0|t}</annotation></semantics></math> lies near mode A, which partially aligns with the prompt, resulting in a small <math id="A1.F11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta_{t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta_{t}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. As the denoising progresses, following the direction of <math id="A1.F11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> leads toward an augmented mode B that even better reflects the prompt semantics. Among the candidate points, <math id="A1.F11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(2)}_{0|t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false" mathsize="1.580em">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(2)}_{0|t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> lies closest to mode B, where the conditional and unconditional predictions are best aligned, yielding a minimal <math id="A1.F11.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta_{t-1}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta_{t-1}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A1.F11.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-loss encourages such behavior.
</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To provide further intuition into <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta_{t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta_{t}\|</annotation></semantics></math> as a navigational tool, we present a 2D illustration depicting two modes of the conditional distribution <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z_{0}\mid c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z_{0}\mid c)</annotation></semantics></math> in Figure <a href="#A1.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ A.4. Intuition for 𝛿-loss ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Navigating with Annealing Guidance Scale in Diffusion Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The point <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0|t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0|t}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the estimated clean image at time <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and the vectors <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional and unconditional noise predictions, respectively (scaling factors omitted for clarity). Their difference, <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}=\epsilon_{t}^{c}-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}=\epsilon_{t}^{c}-\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math>, shown in blue, reflects the guidance direction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At time <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the sample <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0|t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0|t}</annotation></semantics></math> is close to mode A, which corresponds to a high-quality image that partially matches the prompt <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is only slightly biased toward mode B relative to <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math>, leading to a small <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta_{t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta_{t}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">From a navigation perspective, we aim to reach mode B, which even better aligns with the prompt. We consider candidate estimates along the blue dashed line.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The point <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(1)}_{0|t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(1)}_{0|t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the clean image estimate at the next step when a small guidance scale <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is used. At this location, there is a larger gap between <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t-1}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t-1}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t-1}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t-1}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating misalignment.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, the point <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(2)}_{0|t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(2)}_{0|t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which lies near mode B, represents a more optimal solution. Here, both <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t-1}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t-1}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t-1}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t-1}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math> are already aligned toward mode B, resulting in a minimal <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta_{t-1}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta_{t-1}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Our <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-loss leverages this geometric insight during training by encouraging smaller values of <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta_{t-1}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta_{t-1}\|</annotation></semantics></math> through the adaptive selection of the guidance scale <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5. </span>Prompt Perturbation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perturb the conditioning signal solely during training, following CADS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sadat et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. In practice, we apply the noise directly to the prompt embedding <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, using the corruption rule:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}=\sqrt{\gamma(t)}\,c+s\sqrt{1-\gamma(t)}\,n,\quad n\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}=\sqrt{\gamma(t)}\,c+s\sqrt{1-\gamma(t)}\,n,\quad n\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a schedule and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> controls the noise level. We adopt a linear schedule with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{2}=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{2}=T</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> decays from 1 to 0 over the course of denoising, thus inducing higher corruption in earlier timesteps. To maintain the norm of the noised embedding, we rescale the signal as proposed in CADS:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}_{\text{rescaled}}=\frac{\hat{c}-\text{mean}(\hat{c})}{\text{std}(\hat{c})}\,\text{std}(c)+\text{mean}(c),\quad\tilde{c}=\psi\hat{c}_{\text{rescaled}}+(1-\psi)\hat{c}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>rescaled</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>std</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>std</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>rescaled</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{\text{rescaled}}=\frac{\hat{c}-\text{mean}(\hat{c})}{\text{std}(\hat{c})}\,\text{std}(c)+\text{mean}(c),\quad\tilde{c}=\psi\hat{c}_{\text{rescaled}}+(1-\psi)\hat{c},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and set the mixing factor to <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We set the noise scale <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.025" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.025</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.025</annotation></semantics></math>. We ablate this scale by fixing <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.8</annotation></semantics></math> and reporting the performance of the trained scheduler in terms of FID, CLIP similarity, and ImageReward on the COCO2017 Validation set in Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ A.5. Prompt Perturbation ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Navigating with Annealing Guidance Scale in Diffusion Space" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T3.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T3.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">Noise Scale <math id="A1.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T3.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">FID ↓</td>
